# Issue: #106
Feature: Simplify Changed Code
  Apply worthwhile behavior-preserving cleanup to the changed implementation surface.

  Scenario: AC1 current contract
    Given the nmg-sdlc 3.0.0 plugin is installed
    When automated simplify stage exercises this capability
    Then Given changed files, when simplify runs, then it reviews only the bounded diff and directly related context.

  Scenario: AC2 current contract
    Given the nmg-sdlc 3.0.0 plugin is installed
    When automated simplify stage exercises this capability
    Then Given duplicated, indirect, or inefficient code, when cleanup is safe, then it is simplified without altering specified behavior.

  Scenario: AC3 current contract
    Given the nmg-sdlc 3.0.0 plugin is installed
    When automated simplify stage exercises this capability
    Then Given a proposed change alters architecture, security, or acceptance behavior, when considered, then it is left to the owning implementation or verification stage.

  Scenario: AC4 current contract
    Given the nmg-sdlc 3.0.0 plugin is installed
    When automated simplify stage exercises this capability
    Then Given no worthwhile cleanup exists, when review completes, then no weightless refactor is introduced.
